4. State Variables and Operational Definitions

For society i at time t, the core state vector is:

\mathbf{x}_i(t) = (H_i, E_i, S_i, T_i, I_i, R_i, X_i, A_i, D_i)

where the variables are defined as follows.

Variable Definition
H_i Raw advanced human capital: working-age population with advanced scientific, engineering, medical, managerial, or creative capability
E_i Effective energy capacity: reliable electricity consumption per advanced worker
S_i Autonomous scientific capacity: domestic ability to perform frontier-quality research and produce original knowledge
T_i Technological capacity: domestic capacity to design, operate, and improve advanced technologies
I_i Institutional capacity: contract enforcement, research autonomy, merit-based promotion, low corruption
R_i Research ecosystem strength: number and quality of functioning research groups, laboratories, and innovation networks
X_i Infrastructure and connectivity: broadband, transport, laboratory equipment, compute access
A_i Effective AI cognitive service flow per advanced worker, normalized to [0,1]
D_i AI dependency: share of effective AI input sourced from foreign proprietary systems

These definitions remain theoretical. They are intended to be measurable in future empirical work, not estimated here.

