9. Participation Capacity

9.1 Frontier-Normalized ACPC

For society i, the African Civilizational Participation Capacity is defined relative to a global frontier:

ACPC_i(t) = \frac{C_i(t)}{\max_{j \in \mathcal{J}} C_j(t)}
\tag{21}

where \mathcal{J} is the set of all societies included in the comparison.

This normalization avoids the implicit assumption that civilizational capabilities are additively aggregable across countries.

9.2 Continental Distribution

For African societies, the relevant object is not a scalar but a distribution:

\mathbf{ACPC}_{\mathcal{A}}(t) = \{ ACPC_i(t) : i \in \mathcal{A} \}.
\tag{22}

Research should track:

· median participation,
· 25th and 75th percentiles,
· the upper tail of African societies entering high-capability states.

A single continental average obscures more than it reveals.

