## Appendix E. Technical Architecture and Computational Specification

### E.1 Computational Pipeline (Pseudocode)

The following pseudocode specifies how $ACPC_i(t)$ would be computed from calibrated data, for future empirical implementation. No estimation is performed in this paper; this is a specification only.

```
INPUT: 
  raw indicators for society i at time t:
    P_work[i,t], pi1[i,t], pi2[i,t], pi3[i,t]
    E[i,t], I[i,t], X[i,t]
    S[i,t], T[i,t], R[i,t]
    A[i,t], F[i,t], L[i,t]
  calibrated parameters:
    K50[k], rho[k] for k in {E, I, X}
    omega[i,j], rho_S for j in {H_AI, S, T, R}
    theta_local[i], theta_import[i], delta[i], lambda[i], nu_exp[i], Gamma_floor
    a[i], b[i], gamma[i], mu[i], eta[i]

STEP 1: Human capital
  H[i,t] = P_work[i,t] * pi1[i,t] * pi2[i,t] * pi3[i,t]

STEP 2: Dependency
  D[i,t] = F[i,t] / (F[i,t] + L[i,t])

STEP 3: AI augmentation modifier
  theta[i,t] = (1 - D[i,t]) * theta_local[i] + D[i,t] * theta_import[i]
  Gamma_raw = 1 + theta[i,t] * A[i,t]^lambda[i] - delta[i] * A[i,t]^nu_exp[i]
  Gamma[i,t] = max(Gamma_floor, Gamma_raw)

STEP 4: AI-augmented human capital
  H_AI[i,t] = H[i,t] * Gamma[i,t]

STEP 5: Soft-capacity CES aggregation
  Phi[i,t] = ( sum_j omega[i,j] * S_j[i,t]^rho_S )^(1/rho_S)
    where S_j in {H_AI[i,t], S[i,t], T[i,t], R[i,t]}

STEP 6: Hard-constraint gates
  for k in {E, I, X}:
    g[k,i,t] = K[k,i,t]^rho[k] / (K[k,i,t]^rho[k] + K50[k]^rho[k])
  G[i,t] = min( g[E,i,t], g[I,i,t], g[X,i,t] )

STEP 7: Civilizational capability
  C[i,t] = Phi[i,t] * G[i,t]

STEP 8: Frontier normalization
  ACPC[i,t] = C[i,t] / max_j( C[j,t] )   for j in comparison set J

STEP 9: Human-viability screen (reporting flag, not multiplicative)
  viable[i,t] = TRUE if min_k( v_k[i,t] ) >= v_k_min[k] for all k in {1..6}
                else FALSE

OUTPUT: 
  ACPC[i,t], G[i,t], Phi[i,t], D[i,t], viable[i,t]
```

**Design note.** Step 9 is deliberately a *flag*, not a multiplicative factor folded into $C_i$ or $ACPC_i$. This preserves the architecture's requirement (Section 8.4) that human viability be a *binding constraint on the objective function*, not a component that can be traded off against productive capacity inside a single scalar index. Reporting should always present $(ACPC_i, \text{viable}_i)$ as a pair.

### E.2 Data Requirements and Measurability Tiers

| Tier | Variables | Status |
|---|---|---|
| 1 — Operationalizable now | $E_i, X_i, \pi_{i1}$, $v_1$ (fertility), $v_2$ (trust, via survey batteries) | Existing international datasets (energy statistics, enrollment data, demographic and health surveys, World Values Survey–type instruments) |
| 2 — Partially operationalizable | $I_i$ (institutional capacity), $\pi_{i2},\pi_{i3}$, $R_i$, $v_3, v_4, v_5$ | Requires composite indices or proxy construction; substantial measurement-error risk |
